From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: openEuler RISC-V Package Automation <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] build: declare Linux sendfile and CPU affinity interfaces

netlib.c conditionally calls sendfile and sched_setaffinity when configure
detects those functions, but the 2.7.0 source neither includes
sys/sendfile.h nor enables the GNU declarations in sched.h.  GCC 14 rejects
the resulting implicit function declarations.

Define the GNU feature-test macro before the first system header and include
the Linux sendfile header.  This keeps both detected features enabled and
does not affect non-Linux builds.

Patch-Source: Fedora netperf-c99.patch plus openEuler RISC-V package CI failure analysis
Patch-License: MIT
Upstream-Status: Not Submitted (automated upstream writes are not authorized)
---
 src/netlib.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

--- a/src/netlib.c
+++ b/src/netlib.c
@@ -1,2 +1,6 @@
+#if defined(__linux__) && !defined(_GNU_SOURCE)
+#define _GNU_SOURCE 1
+#endif
+
 char    netlib_id[]="\
 @(#)netlib.c (c) Copyright 1993-2012 Hewlett-Packard Company. Version 2.6.0";
@@ -72,6 +76,10 @@ char    netlib_id[]="\
 #endif /* MPE */
 #include <sys/types.h>
 #include <fcntl.h>
+#if defined(__linux__)
+#include <sys/sendfile.h>
+#endif
+
 #include <stdio.h>
 #include <stdlib.h>
 #include <math.h>
